# ─── 3D Memory Album ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env` and fill in:  cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored — never commit real keys.
#
# Only the Express server (server/) reads this file. Vite is never given these
# values, and none of them are prefixed `VITE_`, so no key can end up in a
# browser bundle. The album's UI only ever learns *whether* a provider is
# configured (GET /api/ai/status), never the key itself.
#
# Every key is optional. With none set the app still works end to end: the
# composer chat uses scripted prompts and pages render with the local CSS
# layout instead of an AI image.

# Anthropic — real chat replies + the AI-written journal summary and reflection.
# Without it, the composer falls back to scripted questions and keeps your own
# words as the entry text.  https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Google Gemini — the AI-rendered scrapbook-collage page.
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# OpenAI — the AI-rendered "minimal zine poster" page.
# https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# If both GEMINI_API_KEY and OPENAI_API_KEY are set, the server picks one at
# random per generation so pages vary between the two looks.

# ─── Models ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pinned deliberately: a floating "-latest" alias that gets retired or
# overloaded would silently turn every page into a fallback with no obvious
# cause. Override only if you know you want a different model.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-image
OPENAI_IMAGE_MODEL=gpt-image-1

# ─── Ports ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Port the Express API listens on. The Vite dev server proxies /api here
# (see vite.config.ts); change both together if you move it.
API_PORT=5185
